  "entries": [
    {
      "entry_id": "height-normal-default-opengl",
      "subject": "Normal_OpenGL virtual map from the Height channel, project default method and strength",
      "status": "calibrated",
      "formula": "Input: the stored height h of the Height channel (L16F; the bitmap code c maps to about (2c/65535 - 1) times the layer opacity). In image index space (row 0 is the top row, v up), with wrap-around at the texture borders: dx = h[r,c] - h[r,c-1], dy = h[r,c] - h[r-1,c] (backward differences, one texel). n = normalize(-k dx, k dy, 1), k = 2.56 per unit of height difference at 256 px, computed in float32 (normalize = v * rsqrt(dot(v, v)), rsqrt correctly rounded). Encoding: e = n * 0.5 + 0.5 in float32 for x, y and z. 16-bit code = UNORM16(e): e is truncated to 20 fractional bits (j = floor(e * 2^20)), then code = floor((j * 65535 + 2^19 - 1) / 2^20), the nearest code with ties down (the 0.5 of a flat normal's x and y rounds down). No clamp is needed (e is in [0, 1]). Normal_OpenGL writes (x, y, z) as RGB (y up).",
      "public_sources": [
        {
          "source_id": "P-PBRT",
          "locator": "Bump mapping: displacement gradient by finite differences"
        },
        {
          "source_id": "A-HELP-GUIDE",
          "locator": "Project configuration: normal map format (OpenGL / DirectX)"
        },
        {
          "source_id": "X-D3D12",
          "locator": "Data conversion rules: FLOAT to UNORM"
        }
      ],
      "parameters": [
        {
          "name": "gradient_scale",
          "value": 2.56,
          "origin": "fitted",
          "unit": "per unit height difference at 256 px"
        },
        {
          "name": "difference_kernel",
          "value": [
            -1,
            1
          ],
          "origin": "fitted",
          "unit": "previous texel, current texel"
        },
        {
          "name": "truncation_bits",
          "value": 20,
          "origin": "fitted",
          "unit": "fractional bits"
        },
        {
          "name": "resolution",
          "value": 256,
          "origin": "authored",
          "unit": "px"
        }
      ],
