      "notes": "Domains: the grid2x2 sets (one quad, full 0-1 UVs) compare the whole image, borders included (the wrap-around is exercised there); the sphere and the bevelled cube compare their UV coverage eroded by one texel (58816 and 51040 texels); outside it the export holds padding. Inside the coverage the stored height of the sphere and cube equals that of the plane at opacity 1, so the normal is computed in texture space only (mesh geometry, UV seams and island borders do not enter except through padding read at island edges). Search: forward, central, Sobel-like mixed kernels miss by thousands of codes; the backward one-texel difference with k = 2.56 leaves only +-1 code; k = 2.56 * (1 +- 0.001) gives about 25000 differing values per set. Plain round-to-nearest leaves 1600-2700 values per set 1 code high at fractions 0.5-0.56; truncation to 20 bits before rounding removes them. Remaining +-1 code values (tens per set) sit within 0.06 of a 2^-20 step: float32 rounding of the GPU's rsqrt and multiply order. The scale is fitted at one resolution: whether it is 0.01 x resolution (a UV-space gradient) or fixed per texel is not separable here. The empty Normal channel (base 127/255, 127/255, 1) does not tilt the result: it acts as (0, 0, 1)."
    },
